# Jangou (Japan) - 8x8 character table
# Derived from font bank 00. Glyph tile index = $200 + code, so the 8x8
# charset occupies font tiles $250-$2EF = codes $50-$EF.
# Verified against: bank 05 $9ED2 "<やくまん>", bank 05 $ABB1 "<こしんきろく>"
#
# Dakuten/handakuten are NOT encoded in these codes - they are separate
# combining glyphs living in the $E0 row of the font sheet.
#
# 16x16 kanji use a SEPARATE code space ($00-$93) resolved through the
# translation table at bank 0F $E952. See PHASE1-TEXT-ENGINE.md.

